@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Matched authenticated owner-root experiment
+
+This opt-in fixture compares two frozen native-state producer checkouts. It does
+not change any consumer runtime source, cache bound, or production schedule.
+The initial control is producer `1fe7a0efb10bb8534346b5eb4c8aab3cdf9b0dd2` and
+the consumer base is `6c64b11ec8d277de1cb5b236c5320aa2b9309d13`.
+
+Use the pinned Zig 0.17 toolchain and separate cache/install directories:
+
+```sh
+zig build build-native-owner-root-benchmark \
+  -Dnative-state-path="$OWNER_CONTROL" -Doptimize=safe \
+  -Dtarget=x86_64-linux-gnu.2.35 -Dcpu=baseline+cx16 -j2 \
+  --cache-dir "$OWNER_CONTROL_CACHE" --prefix "$OWNER_CONTROL_BIN"
+zig build build-native-owner-root-benchmark \
+  -Dnative-state-path="$OWNER_TREATMENT" -Doptimize=safe \
+  -Dtarget=x86_64-linux-gnu.2.35 -Dcpu=baseline+cx16 -j2 \
+  --cache-dir "$OWNER_TREATMENT_CACHE" --prefix "$OWNER_TREATMENT_BIN"
+python3 scripts/native_owner_root_benchmark.py \
+  --control "$OWNER_CONTROL_BIN/bin/native-owner-root-benchmark" \
+  --treatment "$OWNER_TREATMENT_BIN/bin/native-owner-root-benchmark" \
+  --output "$OWNER_NEW_EVIDENCE_DIRECTORY"
+```
+
+The Linux driver requires `/usr/bin/time` and an unused output directory. It
+records binary hashes, all process outputs, whole serialized payload/receipt
+bytes, process usage, and host load/pressure every two seconds. Coordinate other
+local builds first. The driver cannot control other users, CPU frequency, or
+unrelated system activity; retain those limitations with any result.
+
+The [fixture](../../test/native_owner_root_benchmark.zig) creates temporary MDBX
+state with 65,536 storage slots. Two distinct-attribute branches execute 64
+transactions writing 128 slots each, followed by one ordinary 21,000-gas
+transaction. Every storage effect and successful record is checked. Both
+branches must reach the unchanged 32,768-entry cap within the 4 MiB RLP
+budget, with actual capacity misses and path fallbacks. Node and provider scratch continue
+through the normal Runtime, Session, and native finalizer.
+
+The ordinary transaction arrives from another task after the primary's last
+bulk append, after that tick's drain phase and before sealing. The rendezvous is
+bounded at five seconds. It deliberately exercises a costly queue phase rather
+than a random arrival distribution. Its nonce is already executable on the
+primary. The primary's physical branch position alternates between the two
+measured observations in every process.
+
+Two schedules are reported separately:
+
+| Schedule | Attempts per turn | Append work allowance | Secondary deferral |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Fixed work | 2 | 1 second | 0 |
+| Deployed Sepolia owner settings | 16 | 20 milliseconds | 250 milliseconds |
+
+Both use ten-millisecond start-to-start pacing. Fixed work must produce exactly
+65 turns and 65 public seals per branch. The driver requires identical native
+read/append/seal counts and all cache statistics except `owner_reads` across
+every fixed-work run. In this fixture the control must count one owner read per
+fallback, while treatment must reuse the authenticated owner and count zero.
+Elapsed-time scheduling can change intermediate seals in the other schedule;
+do not describe its CPU comparison as identical sealing work.
+
+Runtime, Host, and Intake use `SafeAllocator` default options, matching the
+pinned Zig Safe executable's `main(init).gpa`. Test setup and assertion scratch
+still use the test allocator. A separate earlier run with the test runner's
+extra write-after-free checks is ownership evidence, not the same allocator
+performance cohort. Initial inputs are verified and workers initialized before
+each measured Host run; verification of the late transaction is included.
+
+Every complete serialized payload must match byte-for-byte across binaries,
+including state, transaction and receipt roots, block hash, BAL and transaction
+bytes. Reconstructed receipt bytes supplement that authoritative payload
+comparison. An early result remains retained across later revisions; final
+results remain valid after Host stop, Runtime destruction and MDBX teardown.
+The production allocator must be leak-free after all retained results release.
+
+Use three blocks in ABBA, BAAB, ABBA order (`--order`), each with a new evidence
+directory and the same frozen binaries. Each block launches two processes per
+arm. Each process records one warmup
+and two measured observations for each schedule. Excluding warmups gives four
+observations per arm/schedule/block, two per physical primary. Across three
+blocks the independent units are six processes per arm; the two observations
+inside each process are not independent replications. Report adjacent matched
+process differences (T1−C0 and T2−C3 in ABBA, T0−C1 and T3−C2 in BAAB),
+ranges and raw values, not population tail percentiles. Process CPU and seal
+thread CPU are distinct from wall time. State-read time overlaps state-root
+time and must not be added to it.
+
+This is a synthetic saturation stress test: the gas ceiling is 300 million and
+session allowance is 60 seconds. It does not qualify live deadlines, network
+arrival distributions, publisher Prepared time, gossip, proposer receipt, or
+bid outcomes. A local improvement is a reason for subsequent consumer and
+bounded deployment qualification, not evidence of live improvement.
